---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { activities } from '../lib/activities.mjs';
import { QUESTIONS } from '../lib/practice.mjs';
// What each topic's questions cover; the counts come from the question bank itself.
const topics = [
  ['cells', 'Cells', 'Cell structure, organelles, membranes, transport, mitosis and meiosis'],
  ['genetics', 'Genetics', 'Inheritance, blood types, sex linkage, Hardy-Weinberg and evolution'],
  ['molecular', 'Molecular biology', 'DNA, RNA, protein synthesis, enzymes, photosynthesis and respiration'],
  ['ecology', 'Ecology', 'Food webs, energy flow, nutrient cycles, biomes, interactions and populations'],
  ['physiology', 'Human physiology', 'Circulation, breathing, digestion, the nervous system, homeostasis and immunity'],
].map(([key, name, covers]) => [name, covers, QUESTIONS.filter(q => q.topic === key).length]);
---
<Layout title="Biology Worksheets (PDF): Free Printables with Answer Keys" section="Practice" breadcrumbs={[['Biology worksheets', '/worksheets/']]} description="Free printable biology worksheets with answer keys: pick cells, genetics, molecular biology, ecology or physiology and 8, 12 or 20 questions. Save as PDF."><div class="intro"><div><div class="eyebrow">Take the learning with you</div><h1>Free printable biology worksheets with answer keys</h1><p>Choose a topic and a length, and the worksheet builder writes a fresh set of multiple-choice biology questions. Print it or save it as a PDF, with or without the answer key and explanations. It is free for students and teachers, with no sign-up.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="/practice/">Prefer to practice on screen? Start a round ↗</a></div><worksheet-lab><div class="worksheet-controls"><label class="field">Topic<select data-topic><option value="mixed">Mixed topics</option><option value="cells">Cells</option><option value="genetics">Genetics</option><option value="molecular">Molecular biology</option><option value="ecology">Ecology</option><option value="physiology">Human physiology</option></select></label><label class="field">Questions<select data-count><option>8</option><option>12</option><option>20</option></select></label><button class="secondary" data-generate>New question set</button><button class="primary" data-print>Print / save as PDF</button><label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox" data-key checked/> Include answer key</label></div><div class="worksheet-paper" data-paper></div></worksheet-lab><noscript>Enable JavaScript to generate a worksheet. Every topic is also covered in the concept notes and the cell atlas.</noscript><section class="explanation" aria-labelledby="worksheet-topics-heading"><h2 id="worksheet-topics-heading">What is on each biology worksheet</h2><p>Every worksheet is drawn at random from a bank of {QUESTIONS.length} multiple-choice questions, so “New question set” gives a different sheet each time. Each question has four answer choices. The answer key prints after the questions with a short explanation for every answer.</p><div class="fact-table-wrap"><table class="fact-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Topic</th><th scope="col">What the questions cover</th><th scope="col">Questions in the bank</th></tr></thead><tbody>{topics.map(([name, covers, count]) => <tr><td>{name}</td><td>{covers}</td><td>{count}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><h3>How to save a worksheet as a PDF</h3><ol><li>Pick a topic and 8, 12 or 20 questions, and tick or untick “Include answer key”.</li><li>Press “Print / save as PDF”.</li><li>In the print window, choose “Save as PDF” as the printer or destination, with A4 or Letter paper at 100% scale.</li></ol></section>
<section class="explanation" aria-labelledby="worksheet-activities-heading"><h2 id="worksheet-activities-heading">Printable biology activities with answer keys</h2><p>These one-page activities go with the interactive tools: students follow the steps on the sheet, fill in a results table and answer five to seven questions. Teachers will find the answer keys on the <a class="text-link" href="/teachers/">teacher page</a>.</p><ul class="activity-links">{activities.map(act => <li><a class="text-link" href={act.path}>{act.title}</a>: {act.topic.toLowerCase()}, {act.grade.toLowerCase()}, about {act.minutes} minutes</li>)}</ul></section>
<div class="related"><a href="/printable-diagrams/">Printable cell diagrams and Punnett square grids ↗</a><a href="/practice/">Biology practice questions on screen ↗</a><a href="/learn/">Browse the concept notes ↗</a><a href="/teachers/">For teachers ↗</a></div></Layout>
<style>
.activity-links{padding-left:20px;display:grid;gap:4px}
</style>
<script>
import {makeRound} from '../lib/practice.mjs';
class WorksheetLab extends HTMLElement{connectedCallback(){const topic=this.querySelector('[data-topic]') as HTMLSelectElement,count=this.querySelector('[data-count]') as HTMLSelectElement,key=this.querySelector('[data-key]') as HTMLInputElement;const generate=()=>{const round=makeRound(topic.value,Number(count.value));this.querySelector('[data-paper]')!.innerHTML=`<h2>Biology Lab · ${topic.options[topic.selectedIndex].text}</h2><p class="small-note">${round.length} questions · Choose one answer for each. Show your working for any calculation in the space provided.</p><p class="worksheet-print-name">Name: ____________________ &nbsp; Date: ______________</p><ol class="worksheet-questions">${round.map(q=>`<li>${q.q}<div class="worksheet-options">${q.choices.map((c:any,i:number)=>`${'ABCD'[i]}. ${c.text}`).join('<br/>')}</div></li>`).join('')}</ol><section class="worksheet-answers" ${key.checked?'':'hidden'}><h2>Answer key & explanations</h2><ol>${round.map(q=>`<li><strong>${'ABCD'[q.choices.findIndex((c:any)=>c.correct)]}. ${q.choices.find((c:any)=>c.correct).text}</strong><br/>${q.why}</li>`).join('')}</ol></section>`};topic.onchange=generate;count.onchange=generate;key.onchange=()=>{(this.querySelector('.worksheet-answers') as HTMLElement).hidden=!key.checked};(this.querySelector('[data-generate]') as HTMLButtonElement).onclick=generate;(this.querySelector('[data-print]') as HTMLButtonElement).onclick=()=>window.print();generate();}}
customElements.define('worksheet-lab',WorksheetLab);
</script>
